Peer Feedback

Strength
The puzzles are very creative and fun to play. Each house has its own unique mechanic, and the variety keeps players engaged throughout the game.

Risk
The ending feels a bit rushed. The emotional payoff is there, but it comes and goes too quickly. The final scene could be more impactful and leave a stronger impression on the player.

Question about contribution
How did you come up with the ideas for the different puzzles, and what is your plan for improving the ending?

My answer
I came up with most of the puzzle ideas myself based on the theme of each house. The card matching game was inspired by the classic memory match game, and the colorful cube puzzle was inspired by Eggy Party. For the ending, I plan to add more dialogue and slow down the pacing so players have more time to absorb the emotional moment.

Practical suggestion
Extend the ending sequence by adding a few more lines from Granny Meriel, or add a short flashback showing the characters the player has helped throughout the game. This will make the ending feel more earned and memorable.
